  "source": "RMC-BestFit/src/RMC.BestFit/Models/DataFrame/ThresholdDiagnostics.cs @ c2e6192 -- EXACT EMITTER ORACLES dumped from the REAL compiled RMC.BestFit via tools/oracle_emitter and reproduced by tools/verify_oracles.py.",
  "reference": "The two threshold-selection diagnostics for peaks-over-threshold analysis, exposed as threshold_diagnostics() in both packages. Mean residual life is the sample mean of excesses above each candidate threshold with CLT bands (Coles 2001 Section 4.3); parameter stability fits a GPD by MLE at each candidate and reports the modified scale and shape with delta-method bands (Davison and Smith 1990). The dataset is a 200-point GeneralizedPareto(0, 100, 0.1) sample drawn through the ported seeded Mersenne Twister, embedded as a literal. Candidate thresholds below the minimum-exceedance cutoff (5 for MRL, 10 for stability) or with a failed fit are dropped by the core, which is what the two *PointCount cases pin. The stability tolerances are rel 1e-8 (per-threshold MLE fits, so optimizer-dependent, per the file policy); MRL is closed-form and holds rel 1e-10.",
